    <p>Gold’s daily return distribution deviates sharply from normality:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Skewness:</strong> {kpis['skew']:.3f} (moderate left skew — large negative days are more common than large positive days).</li>
      <li><strong>Excess Kurtosis:</strong> {kpis['kurt']:.2f} (fat tails — extreme moves are far more likely than under a normal model).</li>
      <li><strong>Jarque–Bera test:</strong> p &lt; 0.001 → reject normality.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Value-at-Risk (historical):</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>5% daily VaR = <strong>{kpis['var95']*100:.2f}%</strong></li>
